00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.470
Welcome to the MIT
Center for Art, Science,

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:09.170
and Technology's
2021 symposium--

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.380
Unfolding Intelligence,
the Art and Science

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.310
of Contemporary Computation.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.890
CAST was established
in 2012 with the goal

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.440
of building and
building on connections

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.110
between the worlds of art,
science, and technology.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:25.180
This is the third in
a series of symposia

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.370
that CAST has convened
since then, and as

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:31.130
with its predecessors, we bring
together artists, scientists,

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.270
engineers, and humanists
from within MIT

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:36.610
and from the world
at large to discuss

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.590
areas of rapidly
evolving research

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.690
and urgent social relevance.

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:44.200
And defined in that dialogue--
stimulation, confirmation,

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:50.320
provocation, intersection,
and we hope common purpose.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:53.650
At MIT, CAST partners with
departments, labs, and centers

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:56.050
to integrate the arts
across the curriculum,

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:59.590
to enrich and encourage artistic
collaboration, and to provide

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:02.710
support to faculty and
members of the MIT community

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:04.960
as they pursue their
own artistic practice

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.870
and/or research.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:09.910
In addition to
symposia like this,

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:12.490
CAST facilitates the sharing
of this creative work

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:14.980
beyond the Institute
by producing concerts,

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.590
exhibitions, and
publications and making

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:20.270
them available to the public.

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:22.910
So thank you for
being with us today.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.910
We hope you will join
us throughout the week

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:28.270
at virtual events addressing
the aesthetic, technical,

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:31.600
and critical issues pertaining
to artificial intelligence

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.970
and computational media.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:37.630
We also look forward to seeing
you on Friday, April 9th,

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:41.440
as the symposium culminates
with a live interactive event

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.690
to which all
attendees are invited,

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:46.240
and which you can join
presenters and artists

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:49.810
in breakout rooms to explore
hidden threads between all that

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.430
has been discussed this week.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:10.700
Hello.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:17.660
